  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ethiopia Elections and Political Processes Activity (EEPPA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CEPPS seeks to build political will and institutional capacity for competitive, peaceful elections, as well as inclusive, responsive, democratic governance. To do this, CEPPS works directly with the National Election Board of Ethiopia (NEBE), civil society organizations, media, and political parties, in order to strengthen the participation of all citizens throughout their political systems, including women, youth, and other traditionally marginalized groups. Additionally, CEPPS promotes the integrity of Ethiopian elections to peacefully and democratically select leaders; to better harness the medias capability to promote citizens political understanding, and transparency within the electoral process, as well as to improve competitive, representative multiparty political systems.</narrative>
  </description>
